# Do not duplicate stylesheet metrics in C++

When C++ needs a pixel size, query the live style after polish. Do not copy padding, border, or radius values from `theme_light.qss`. Those tokens will drift and clip text.

```cpp
// BAD — lg padding 24+24 and a guessed focus ring
constexpr int horizontalPaddingPx = 48;
constexpr int focusBorderSlackPx = 4;
return textWidth + horizontalPaddingPx + focusBorderSlackPx;

// GOOD — QStyle applies current QSS box model (including :focus)
button->ensurePolished();
QStyleOptionButton option;
option.initFrom(button);
option.state |= QStyle::State_HasFocus;
option.text = button->text();
const QSize textSize = button->fontMetrics().size(Qt::TextShowMnemonic, button->text());
return button->style()->sizeFromContents(QStyle::CT_PushButton, &option, textSize, button).width();
```

Recompute on `StyleChange` / `FontChange` / text changes. Prefer `sizeFromContents`, `pixelMetric`, or `contentsMargins()` over magic numbers. Keep visual tokens in QSS (`Style::setSize` / `setVariant`).
